# videoModel - what never belongs in this repository
#
# The rule this file follows: everything reproducible by run_all.py from the
# dataset stays out; the code, the two JSON files that define the vocabulary
# and the phrases, and the artefacts a reviewer needs to check a claim are in.
#
# (gitignore has no inline comments: a # after a pattern is part of the
#  pattern, which is why every note here sits on its own line)

# --- data: a ~70 GB manual download with third-party terms ------------------
# Never committed, never moved, never written to. See ASL_Citizen/use.txt.
ASL_Citizen/
datasets/*
!datasets/.gitkeep
longVideos/*

# --- generated by the pipeline ----------------------------------------------
# cache/              landmark .npy files, manifest.csv, extract_errors.csv
# logs/               one log per run
# models/checkpoints/ resumable training state (train_state.pt)
cache/
logs/
models/checkpoints/
# User-run experiments stay local until a validated candidate is adopted.
candidates/

# the MediaPipe Holistic graph (13,683,609 bytes) is fetched once into models/
# by src/landmarks.py, or pointed at with ASL_WORDS_HOLISTIC_MODEL. Too big for
# a commit for something that downloads in seconds.
models/holistic_landmarker.task

# --- partial writes: save() writes these and renames them, so a leftover
# --- means an interrupted run, never a file worth keeping
*.part
*.npy.part

# --- python and editor noise ------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- per-seed bulk: 276 files that are one copy of the same report per seed -
# reports/seeds/<tag>-seed<n>/   each holds predictions/per_word/confusion/...
# for one seed of one sweep. The promoted seed's copies are what get promoted
# into reports/ (and into REPORT_WORDS.md), and reports/seed_runs.csv holds the
# mean+-spread for every seed that ever ran - so nothing is lost by leaving the
# folders out. They are rebuilt by python -m src.train --seeds 3.
reports/seeds/

# --- kept on this machine only -----------------------------------------------
# the losing feature-vector checkpoint, retrainable with --feature-version 2
# and named in README.md / docs/DETAILS.md
models/words_v3.pt
# the word drill page points at dataset clips with absolute file:///D:/ paths,
# so it is only usable on the machine that has the datasets
drill_cards.html

# --- what IS SHIPPED, and why a clone needs no training and no re-running ---
#   models/words_core20.pt     1.5 MB   the weights
#   models/words_core20.onnx   ~1.5 MB  the exported graph
#   models/meta.json                    labels, dims, splits, seed, licence
#   reports/words_summary.json          the compact numbers
#   reports/per_word*.csv               per-word accuracy with counts
#   reports/confusion_words*.csv        the confusion matrix
#   reports/confused_pairs*.csv         the pairs the model swaps
#   reports/predictions*.csv            one row per sample: which signer, which
#                                       clip, what probability - the evidence
#                                       behind every percentage
#   REPORT_WORDS.md                     the human-readable result
# No pattern above matches any of those, so they stay tracked.
